		DVB-S2X VL-SNR Modulator/Demodulator
		====================================

This is a C implementation of the DVB-S2X Very Low Signal-to-Noise Ratio
(VL-SNR) physical layer as specified in ETSI EN 302 307-2.  All 9 MODCODs
are implemented, covering the operating range from -2 dB to -10 dB Es/N0.

The library provides a complete transmit and receive chain including FEC
(BCH + LDPC), pi/2-BPSK and QPSK modulation, symbol spreading, pilot
insertion, PL scrambling, RRC pulse shaping, symbol timing recovery,
carrier frequency/phase recovery, and frame synchronization.


Building
--------

	make			Build libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a
	make DEBUG=1		Debug build (-g -O0)
	make test		Build and run all tests
	make clean		Remove objects and binaries

Requirements: GCC with C11 support, libm.  No external dependencies.


Directory Layout
----------------

	include/		Public headers
	src/			Library source
	tables/			LDPC parity-check address tables
	test/			Test programs

The build produces a single static library: libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a


Supported MODCODs
-----------------

  Index  Modulation     Rate   FEC     Spread  Es/N0 threshold
  -----  ----------     ----   -----   ------  ---------------
    1    QPSK           2/9    64800     no       -3 dB
    2    pi/2-BPSK      1/5    32400     no       -6 dB
    3    pi/2-BPSK      11/45  32400     no       -5 dB
    4    pi/2-BPSK      1/3    32400     no       -4 dB
    5    pi/2-BPSK      1/5    16200     x2       -9 dB
    6    pi/2-BPSK      11/45  16200     x2       -8 dB
    7    pi/2-BPSK      1/5    16200     no       -6 dB
    8    pi/2-BPSK      4/15   16200     no       -5 dB
    9    pi/2-BPSK      1/3    16200     no       -4 dB

Thresholds are measured through the full RF chain (RRC + timing offset
0.30 symbol + frequency offset 1e-4 cycles/symbol + phase offset 0.7 rad
+ AWGN) at FER < 1e-2.


Signal Chain
------------

Transmitter:

	User data -> BB frame -> BCH encode -> LDPC encode ->
	bit interleave -> modulate (pi/2-BPSK or QPSK) ->
	symbol spread (MODCODs 5,6 only) ->
	PL frame assembly (PL header + WH header + pilots) ->
	PL scramble (data field only) -> RRC pulse shape

Receiver:

	RRC matched filter -> Oerder-Meyr timing recovery ->
	frame sync (segment-coherent WH correlation) ->
	coarse frequency (L&R, SNR-gated) ->
	residual carrier track (WH + pilot linear phase fit) ->
	PL descramble -> pilot extract -> despread ->
	soft demap (LLR) -> deinterleave ->
	LDPC decode (sum-product) -> BCH decode -> BB frame parse


Public API
----------

The public interface is defined in include/dvbs2x_vlsnr.h.  Link against
libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a and libm.

All functions return 0 on success, -1 on error unless noted otherwise.


1. Initialization

	#include "dvbs2x_vlsnr.h"

	struct dvbs2x_modulator mod;
	struct dvbs2x_demodulator demod;

	dvbs2x_modulator_init(&mod, modcod_idx, rolloff, sps, scrambling_idx);
	dvbs2x_demodulator_init(&demod, rolloff, sps, scrambling_idx);

  modcod_idx	MODCOD index, 1 through 9 (see table above).
  rolloff	RRC roll-off factor.  Use 0.35 (DVB-S2X Annex D default)
		or 0.20 / 0.25 / 0.10 per system configuration.
  sps		Samples per symbol.  Minimum 2.
  scrambling_idx  PL scrambling sequence index, 0-7.  Use 0 for default.


2. Modulation (RF output)

	struct dvbs2x_complex *output;
	unsigned int out_len;

	output = malloc(cap * sizeof(struct dvbs2x_complex));
	dvbs2x_modulate(&mod, user_data, user_bits, output, &out_len);

  user_data	Input bit array (uint8_t, one bit per byte, values 0/1).
  user_bits	Number of user data bits.  Maximum is k_bch - 80 for the
		selected MODCOD (80 bits reserved for BB frame header).
  output	Caller-allocated buffer for complex baseband IQ samples
		at the configured samples-per-symbol rate.
  out_len	Receives the number of output samples written.

  The output buffer must be large enough to hold the full frame.  A safe
  upper bound is:

	cap = (DVBS2X_PLHEADER_LEN + DVBS2X_VLSNR_HDR_LEN +
	       mc->fec_len * 2 +
	       (mc->fec_len * 2 / 1440 + 1) * 36 + 64) * sps;


3. Modulation (symbol-rate output)

	struct dvbs2x_complex *symbols;
	unsigned int sym_len;

	dvbs2x_modulate_symbols(&mod, user_data, user_bits,
				symbols, &sym_len);

  Same as dvbs2x_modulate() but produces symbol-rate output without RRC
  pulse shaping.  Useful for simulation at symbol level or when the pulse
  shaping is handled externally (e.g. by an FPGA or SDR front-end).


4. Demodulation (RF input)

	uint8_t *user_out;
	unsigned int rec_len;

	user_out = malloc(mc->k_bch);
	ret = dvbs2x_demodulate(&demod, input, in_len, user_out, &rec_len);

  input		Complex baseband IQ samples at the configured sps rate.
		The buffer must contain at least one complete PL frame.
  in_len	Number of input samples.
  user_out	Receives decoded user data bits (one bit per byte).
  rec_len	Receives the number of user bits recovered.

  Returns 0 if LDPC and BCH decoding both succeed, -1 otherwise.
  On failure, user_out may contain partially decoded (unreliable) data.

  The demodulator performs matched filtering, symbol timing recovery,
  frame synchronization, carrier recovery, and FEC decoding internally.


5. Demodulation (symbol-rate input)

	ret = dvbs2x_demodulate_symbols(&demod, symbols, sym_len,
					noise_var, user_out, &rec_len);

  symbols	Complex symbols at 1 sample/symbol (post matched filter,
		post timing recovery).
  sym_len	Number of input symbols.
  noise_var	Per-component noise variance estimate.  Pass 0.0 to use
		the internal estimator (second-difference method).
  user_out	Receives decoded user data bits.
  rec_len	Receives the number of user bits recovered.

  This is the symbol-level receiver core.  Use it when timing recovery
  and matched filtering are handled externally, or for back-to-back
  simulation without RF impairments.


6. MODCOD query

	const struct dvbs2x_modcod *mc;

	mc = dvbs2x_vlsnr_get_modcod(modcod_idx);

  Returns a pointer to the MODCOD parameter structure for the given
  index (1-9), or NULL if the index is out of range.  The structure
  contains all code parameters (k_bch, fec_len, code_rate, etc.).

  User data capacity per frame:  mc->k_bch - 80  bits.


Minimal Example
---------------

	#include "dvbs2x_vlsnr.h"
	#include <stdlib.h>

	int main(void)
	{
		struct dvbs2x_modulator mod;
		struct dvbs2x_demodulator demod;
		const struct dvbs2x_modcod *mc;
		struct dvbs2x_complex *iq;
		uint8_t *tx_data, *rx_data;
		unsigned int tx_bits, out_len, rx_len;
		unsigned int cap, i;

		/* Select MODCOD 5: BPSK 1/5 spread, -9 dB capable */
		dvbs2x_modulator_init(&mod, 5, 0.35, 2, 0);
		dvbs2x_demodulator_init(&demod, 0.35, 2, 0);

		mc = dvbs2x_vlsnr_get_modcod(5);
		tx_bits = mc->k_bch - 80;

		tx_data = calloc(tx_bits, 1);
		rx_data = calloc(mc->k_bch, 1);
		cap = 80000;
		iq = calloc(cap, sizeof(*iq));

		/* Fill with test pattern */
		for (i = 0; i < tx_bits; i++)
			tx_data[i] = i & 1;

		/* Transmit */
		dvbs2x_modulate(&mod, tx_data, tx_bits, iq, &out_len);

		/* ... channel (add noise, offsets, etc.) ... */

		/* Receive */
		if (dvbs2x_demodulate(&demod, iq, out_len,
				      rx_data, &rx_len) == 0)
			/* rx_data[0..rx_len-1] matches tx_data */

		free(tx_data);
		free(rx_data);
		free(iq);
		return 0;
	}

Compile:

	gcc -Iinclude -o example example.c -L. -ldvbs2x_vlsnr -lm


Test Programs
-------------

  test_modulator	Unit tests for individual blocks (BCH, LDPC, RRC,
			PL header, scrambler, modulation).

  test_loopback		Noiseless loopback for all 9 MODCODs at symbol level.
			Verifies the encode/decode chain produces zero errors.

  test_e2e		End-to-end modulator pipeline check.  Verifies frame
			lengths and RRC output for all MODCODs.

  test_api_loopback	Public API loopback with configurable impairments.
			Usage: test_api_loopback [modcod] [esn0] [mode] [seed]
			       [freq] [phase] [timing]
			mode 0 = symbol level, mode 1 = full RF.

  test_ber		BER waterfall for a single MODCOD (symbol level).
			Usage: test_ber [modcod] [frames_per_point]

  test_ber_vlsnr	BER test with puncturing/shortening active.
			Exercises the native-rate LDPC at low Es/N0.

  test_rf_ber		Full RF chain BER characterization for all 9 MODCODs.
			Applies timing, frequency, phase offsets and AWGN.
			Usage: test_rf_ber [modcod] [frames_per_point]


Implementation Notes
--------------------

LDPC Decoder:

  The decoder uses a layered sum-product (belief propagation) schedule
  with the exact box-plus check-node update.  This recovers approximately
  2 dB compared to normalized min-sum, which matters at VL-SNR operating
  points.  LLR values are clamped to +/-40 to prevent numerical overflow.
  Maximum iterations default to 50 (DVBS2X_LDPC_MAX_ITER).

  The parity-check matrix is stored in Compressed Sparse Row (CSR) format,
  built from the quasi-cyclic address tables in tables/.

Frame Synchronization:

  The 896-symbol VL-SNR Walsh-Hadamard header is correlated using a
  segment-coherent algorithm: the header is divided into 128-symbol
  segments, each correlated coherently, and the segment magnitudes are
  summed.  This tolerates residual frequency offsets up to approximately
  1/(4*128) = 2e-3 cycles/symbol during acquisition.

Carrier Recovery:

  Two-stage approach:
  1. Coarse: Luise-Reggiannini autocorrelation estimator on the WH
     header, gated by an SNR threshold (disabled below 4 dB estimated
     Es/N0 to avoid noise-induced drift).
  2. Fine: weighted linear fit of unwrapped phase measurements from the
     WH header and all pilot blocks across the frame.  The header
     anchors the phase; the pilots provide the long baseline for
     residual frequency estimation.

Timing Recovery:

  Feed-forward Oerder-Meyr (square-and-DFT) estimator with 4-point
  cubic (Catmull-Rom) interpolation.  This is a non-data-aided,
  open-loop estimator that works reliably at very low SNR without
  the symbol-slipping problems of a Gardner timing loop.


References
----------

  ETSI EN 302 307-1 V1.4.1	DVB-S2 base standard
  ETSI EN 302 307-2 V1.3.1	DVB-S2X extensions (VL-SNR in clause 5.5.2)
  ETSI TR 102 376-1 V1.2.1	DVB-S2 implementation guidelines
  ETSI TR 102 376-2 V1.2.1	DVB-S2X implementation guidelines


